            <div xml:id="d807">

                <pb facs="0775" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.24/1229: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-12-14">December 14,
                        1941</date>.<lb/>[Received December 14—5:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6050. Our 5743, [November] 28.<anchor n="54" xml:id="d807-f1"/> Following
                    informal Foreign Office note, dated December 13th, received today: <pb
                        facs="0776" n="766" xml:id="pg766"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“On 8th November you raised with me the exemption from import duty of
                            Lend-Lease equipment imported into Burma for the assembly of Lend-Lease
                            materials for China and also of Lend-Lease trucks imported into Burma
                            for the transport of Lend-Lease materials to China.</p>
                        <p>I am now glad to be able to inform you that arrangements have been made
                            to exempt such materials from duty on importation into Burma. There
                            remains the question of how these materials are ultimately to be
                            disposed of, but this I suggest can be left for discussion at a later
                            date.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
